  "designDirection": {
    "acceptance": [
      "Pages feel calm, warm, and complete through white paper, thin headings on one scale, and helpful language.",
      "Visitors can understand the content and identify the next action quickly.",
      "Red appears only as identity and signal: the logo, link and menu rules, focus, and at most one highlighter stroke.",
      "Every page starts light, only the user switches it to dark, and the top menu fits in five items.",
      "Forms and technical content remain clear, readable, and easy to scan.",
      "Brand identity, keyboard focus, reduced motion, and supported themes remain intact."
    ],
    "avoid": [
      "Red buttons, red statistics, red fills, or red text. The logo and the one highlighter stroke are the only red areas",
      "More than one highlighter stroke on a page",
      "Uppercase labels, eyebrow labels, arrows on buttons, or decorative motion",
      "Inflated luxury claims or forced friendliness",
      "A primary button in every section, card, or list",
      "A sidebar on a website, or more than five items in its top menu",
      "A theme that follows the device setting, or a page that starts dark",
      "Lifestyle photography or a photograph behind body text"
    ],
    "definition": "Scandinavian restraint filtered through Mediterranean warmth.",
    "intent": "Create minimal, functional, and elegant experiences that feel calm, warm, and human.",
    "invariants": [
      {
        "datasheet": "The lockup at the top left of every sheet.",
        "linkedin": "The lockup at the foot of every post image; the avatar is the symbol tile.",
        "rule": "One symbol and a lowercase wordmark in the identity ink. Never redrawn, never with a tagline.",
        "web": "The site lockup in the top menu and the footer."
      },
      {
        "datasheet": "No red, except the Ağustos logo.",
        "linkedin": "No red, except the Ağustos logo and at most one highlighter stroke in the headline.",
        "rule": "Red is identity and signal only: the Ağustos logo, and on screen the link rule, focus and one marker stroke. Never a fill, a button or text colour.",
        "web": "The logo, the 2px link and menu rule, keyboard focus and one highlighter stroke per page. Buttons are black."
      },
      {
        "datasheet": "The same faces and weights at the print sizes of recipes.document.",
        "linkedin": "The headline takes the H1 role, the deck the deck role.",
        "rule": "Three faces on one scale: Inter Tight for headings, Inter for text, JetBrains Mono for data. Headings are thin and in sentence case.",
        "web": "The type table (recipes.typeRoles) through the kit classes."
      },
      {
        "datasheet": "Every spec row.",
        "linkedin": "Any figure that appears in a post image.",
        "rule": "Spec values are data: mono figures with the unit, the label in the display face.",
        "web": "type-spec on the spec table or list."
      },
      {
        "datasheet": "White A4, wide margins, one product title.",
        "linkedin": "A white field; the headline is the only large text.",
        "rule": "White paper and generous space. One title opens the page and nothing sits above it.",
        "web": "White paper, the section spacing, one closing band."
      },
      {
        "datasheet": "Sentence case labels; Turkish with lang=tr.",
        "linkedin": "One idea per post image, in sentence case.",
        "rule": "Plain, short, active words. No all-caps labels, no label above a title, no inflated claims.",
        "web": "Sentence case in headings, menus and buttons."
      },
      {
        "datasheet": "Ink and ink-soft on white only.",
        "linkedin": "Ink on white only; no text on a photograph.",
        "rule": "Text clears 4.5:1 contrast and graphics 3:1 (WCAG 2.2 AA).",
        "web": "The states table; the build refuses a failing pair."
      }
    ],
    "keywords": [
      "calm",
      "clear",
      "warm",
      "functional",
      "elegant",
      "approachable",
      "grounded",
      "quietly confident"
    ],
    "name": "İskandivvian",
    "naming": "Use this as a defined project label, not an established design movement.",
    "principles": [
      "Use six colours: white #ffffff as the paper, pale red #fdf5f5 for the closing band, light gray #ebebeb for functional surfaces, dark gray #404040 for secondary text, off-black #15130f for text and buttons, and red #cf142a. Two support values serve only hairlines (#e8e4da) and faint marks (#8a8378). A new value needs a deleted one.",
      "Set type on one golden scale: the 16.5px body times 1.272 per step, so every second step is the golden ratio (13, 16.5, 21, 27, 34, 43, 55, 70, 89px). Headings are thin: hero 89px light, H1 55px light, H2 43px regular, H3 21px medium. Use four weights (300, 400, 500, 600). The wordmark alone uses 650.",
      "Use two radii, 6px for controls and 12px for cards, and one section spacing. Do not use gradients or textures. The only shadow sits under a menu that floats above the page.",
      "Red is identity and signal, never action: the logo, the 2px link and menu rule, keyboard focus, and one highlighter stroke per page. Buttons are black. The Ağustos logo is red and turns black on hover; every other house brand's logo is black and turns red on hover.",
      "Use the highlighter on one to four words of the main headline: once on the homepage, at most once on any other page. Never on links, buttons, numbers, body text, or product UI. The sentence must read the same without it.",
      "Websites use the top menu with at most five items. Extra pages go under one More menu, and social, legal, and language links live in the footer. Product UI uses the sidebar, or the top menu when it has about ten destinations or fewer. Every page starts light. A site may add a theme switch; the user picks dark, never the device.",
      "Copy a screen; do not design a page. Open with a headline, a deck, two buttons, and a trust line. Close with one pale red band.",
      "Bold (600) marks a fact the reader scans for, at most once per paragraph. Italic marks names of publications and projects, foreign terms, and quoted phrases. Underline is for links only. Do not combine them, and do not use uppercase labels, eyebrow headings, or coloured text.",
      "When unsure, do the conventional thing. Collect design tweaks and release the kit once a month; fix real defects at once."
    ]
  },
